# Env files: deny by default, allow only the ones that are genuinely public.
#
# .env.uat holds EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* values. Those are PUBLIC by
# construction — every one of them is inlined into the client bundle and
# readable by anyone who opens the app. They identify the project; they
# authorise nothing. Access is controlled by firestore.rules and Firebase
# Auth. Committing them is what makes `npm run build:web:uat` reproducible
# for anyone else on the team.
#
# Anything else matching .env* stays ignored, so a future file holding a real
# secret (an admin key, a Twilio token) is excluded unless someone
# deliberately adds an exception here.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.uat

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

# tests
coverage/

# misc
*.log


../../../.env*
